  "text": "t0 00\n.00 70.00 23 ar reek\nB'ATETIMTAMINLНЧEMА BIlI\nORDINANCE NO. 7-A\nAN ORDINANCE TO REPEAL ORDINANCE NO. T\nWHEREAS, C.R.S. §30-28-111 et seq., authorizes boards of county commissioners to plan for\nand regulate the use of land; and\nWHEREAS, C.R.S. §30-28-111 et seq., authorizes boards of county commissioners to adopt and\namend zoning regulations pursuant to specified procedures for the purposes of promoting health,\nsafety, morals, convenience, order, prosperity or welfare of the present and future inhabitants of\nthe county; and\nWHEREAS, C.R.S. §30-28-116 authorizes boards of county commissioners to amend county\nzoning regulations pursuant to specified procedures; and\nWHEREAS, the County has heretofore enacted Ordinance No. 7 which purports to adopt the\nC.R.S.§30-28-124 and C.R.S. §30-28-124.5 dealing with penalties as they relate to zoning\nviolations and establishes policies and procedures for zoning enforcement; and,\nWHEREAS, the County has the authority to enforce the provisions of C.R.S. §30-28-124 and\nC.R.S. §30-28-124.5 without its adoption via Ordinance making Ordinance No. 7 cumulative and\nunnecessary; and\nWHEREAS, the Board of County Commissioners believes that it is in the best interest of the\nCitizens of the County to repeal Ordinance No. 7.\nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED that Ordinance No. 7 is hereby repealed in full.\nINTRODUCED, FIRST READ, ORDERED PUBLISHED IN FULL AND SET FOR PUBLIC\nHEARING THIS6TH\n_DAY OF JUNE, 2007.\nBOARD OF COUNTY COMMISSIONERS\nCLEAR CREEK COUNTY\nbanN\nFoan Drury, Chairman\nAbsent\nKevin J. O'Malley, Commissioner\nAode E\nHarry Dale, Commissioner\nATTEST:\nExthutther\nDeputy Clerk and Recorder\nAPPROVED AS FO FORM:\nOllen\nICOEA\nRobert W. Loeffler, County Attorney\nG:IDEPTDATAIWP51 \\ATTORNEY\\PATRICKIMy Projects\\Zoning Enforcement DepartmentOrdinance 7A.wpd\nPage 1",
